```java
class Cart {
    List<CartItem> items;

    Order checkout(PaymentMethod payment) {
        List<OrderItem> orderItems = items.stream()
            .map(ci -> new OrderItem(
                ci.product.id,
                ci.product.name,          // snapshot, not a live lookup
                ci.product.currentPrice,  // frozen at this instant
                ci.quantity,
                ci.selectedOptions))
            .toList();

        for (OrderItem item : orderItems) {
            inventory.reserve(item.productId, item.quantity);
        }

        Order order = orderRepo.create(orderItems, OrderStatus.PLACED);
        paymentService.charge(payment, order.total());
        return order;
    }
}
```

The `.name` and `.currentPrice` reads happen once, at checkout, and are copied by value into `OrderItem` — nothing about the resulting `Order` changes if `Product` is edited afterward.
